<EVENT VALUE="STOPMOVIE">
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="4">"They say there are 62,000 species of mushrooms in the world. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">So even when we just say mushrooms, they vary widely in size and appearance. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">What's growing over there is the part of the fungus called the </STYLE><STYLE ID="9" RUBY="しじつたい">fruiting body</STYLE><STYLE ID="4">―</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">that is, the part of the fungus proper that corresponds to the mushroom. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">So you could say there's a much bigger main body hidden underground."</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="4">"When I was assigned to the International Research Institute, what I worked on was research into a cherry tree here in Motoki City. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">Only... that International Research Institute had a bit of a hidden side to it. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">It existed to investigate and research phenomena that couldn't be made public."</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="2">"</STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Goto</STYLE><STYLE ID="2">, are you allowed to tell us that...?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="4">"It's fine. The researchers are probably all dead by now. I'm out of a job too."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"............"</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="4">"That research that couldn't be made public was research on the goshinboku that grew in Central Park. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">I don't know the details myself, but 70 years ago, when that cherry tree sprang up, people tried to study it and all the researchers died. It's a cherry tree with a dark history."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"I had no idea about any of that..."</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="4">"Well, it's been covered up at the national level until now."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"So that goshinboku was that dangerous..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="4">"Yes. That goshinboku was itself a fungus disguised as a cherry tree. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">I started by collecting the pollen drifting in the air, without touching the goshinboku's flowers. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">And it turned out the goshinboku's pollen wasn't pollen, but spores."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"Spores... those are what mold and moss grow from, right?"</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="4">"Yes, but the goshinboku's spores are a little unusual: they don't germinate under any conditions. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">Spores are what seeds are to plants, so normally they germinate one way or another. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">But my experiments to germinate the airborne spores all ended in failure."</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="4">"Next I collected branches that had fallen around the goshinboku and fragments of root that had broken off above ground and examined them, and the roots contained spores too. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">Unlike the airborne spores, the root spores germinate when they enter a mammal's body. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">Even when they germinate, they don't grow bigger than a few microns. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">These germinated spores release a substance similar to ephedrine inside the body."</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="4">"Ephedrine acts strongly on the human sympathetic nervous system. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">In other words, this ephedrine-like substance has an effect equal to or greater than adrenaline. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">When that happens, do you know what effect it has on the human body?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"I have no idea..."</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\プリズン\五島マンションリビング.gal" "NORMAL" "" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
